Z||000000||fierospeeder||08-07-2001||04:05 AM||||Anyone see this on the news.  <P>I think it was a full size van that broke down in the left side of the highway.  I cant tell if it was on the road.  So a car slams into it, and causes a chain reaction.  All the other drivers having the "right to speed" cant avoid the crash and run into it.  One guy in a jap car, is doing 360s trying to control his car, guess he needs bigger sway bars?<P>Is this a common thing? ive seen a lot of accident videos of people hitting parked cars.  When a vehicle is getting bigger in size, it is moving away from you!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-07-2001||11:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierospeeder:<BR><B>I think it was a full size van that broke down in the left side of the highway.  I cant tell if it was on the road.  So a car slams into it, and causes a chain reaction.  All the other drivers having the "right to speed" cant avoid the crash and run into it. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As long as there wasn't a box of kittens in the van.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Is this a common thing?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes. People are eating, drinking, putting on makeup, talking on the cell phone, fiddling with the radio, talking to the kids in the back seat and not driving.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||08-07-2001||11:13 AM||||Anyone remember the VOLVO commercials;<P>Guy eating cereal/breakfast in car.<BR>Old lady getting licked by her dog.<BR>etc...if there was more<P>"They are out there" I believe was VOLVO's motto.<P>I also seen the accident this morning before heading off to work on the All News Channel (ANC).  Wicked!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But Sad!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'm just happy to hear that no one was seriously injured or killed.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||08-07-2001||11:18 AM||||people in CA drive WAY too close to the cars infront of them for the speeds they are going - like 1 car length at 70mph - all of them (Im not kidding)<P>  I was out there on business for a week once, had a rental car, and almost got into 3 accidents - Im talking about getting missed by a few inches<P>  So a chain reaction pileup is pretty much what you would expect to happen out there if anything happens on the highway.||||reg||10
